From 110c5ca5f43f48c8e717ecf3780e9f4bcda65d53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aadilparmar <124196983+aadilparmar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Apr 2026 12:22:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] security: server-side admin auth with HttpOnly cookie +
 requireAdmin guard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Previously every /api/admin/* route was publicly callable — anyone could
POST to /api/admin/settings and modify the site. Admin "auth" was a
SHA-256 hash hardcoded in the client bundle with a sessionStorage flag,
trivially bypassable in DevTools. This commit wires real auth through
the unused admin_sessions table that was already in the schema.

- New lib/auth.ts: requireAdmin(), getAdminFromRequest(),
  adminCookieHeader/clearAdminCookieHeader, destroyAdminSession.
  Single indexed query per request.
- /api/admin/login sets HttpOnly SameSite=Lax Secure cookie on success
  and no longer returns the token in the response body.
- New /api/admin/logout (clears cookie + deletes DB row) and
  /api/admin/me (cheap session verify for UI gating).
- requireAdmin() guard added to 12 admin routes + /api/dashboard/stats.
  Bot probes now get 401 before any DB work.
- AdminLogin calls POST /api/admin/login; AdminShell and settings
  Logout call /api/admin/logout.
- iww-hq/layout verifies session via /api/admin/me on mount.
- Drop the hardcoded password hash and verifyCredentials from the
  client bundle. sessionStorage stays only as a pure UX hint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
